    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d768-a1">

                <pb facs="1227" n="1131" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg1131"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No.
                    139.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Raschid Pasha to Mr.
                            Boker.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Sublime Porte, Department of Foreign
                            Affairs</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1873-08-21"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 21,
                        1873</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit yon herein
                    inclosed a copy of my last circular forwarded to the representatives of the
                    Sublime Porte abroad, with the instruction to notify the governments to which
                    they are accredited of the date of the convocation of the international
                    commission which is to meet at Constantinople with the view of determining a
                    unification of tonnage.</p>
                <p>In the absence of the incumbent of the imperial legation at Washington, I deemed
                    it proper to have recourse to your mediation in forwarding this notification to
                    the United States Government. I shall therefore be much obliged if, considering
                    the urgency of the matter, you will communicate by telegraph to the cabinet of
                    Washington the object of the dispatch in question. Accept, sir, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>RASCHID.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
